👨‍💻 Project Overview

This repository contains my Lab 17 Final Project from the Hands-On Introduction to Linux Commands, Shell Scripting, and Operating Systems course.

The project focuses on developing a fully automated Linux backup solution using Bash scripting. The script identifies files modified within the last 24 hours, archives them into a compressed backup file, and stores the backup in a specified destination directory.

Through this project, I applied practical Linux administration skills, shell scripting concepts, file management operations, process automation, and task scheduling techniques.

🎯 Project Objectives

The objectives of this project were to:

Develop a Bash shell script for automated backups.
Practice Linux file and directory operations.
Work with command-line arguments.
Implement variables and arithmetic operations.
Use conditional statements and loops.
Create compressed archive files using tar.
Schedule automated tasks using cron.
Strengthen Linux system administration skills.

