📜 Backup Script Features

The backup script performs the following tasks:

✅ Accepts source and destination directories as command-line arguments

✅ Validates user input

✅ Calculates timestamps

✅ Identifies files modified within the last 24 hours

✅ Stores eligible files in an array

✅ Compresses files into a .tar.gz archive

✅ Moves backup files to the destination directory

✅ Supports automation using Cron Jobs

🔍 Project Implementation
Task 1: Define Directory Variables

Created variables to store command-line arguments.

targetDirectory=$1
destinationDirectory=$2
![Task 1](screenshots/task1-directory-variables.png)

Task 2: Display Command-Line Arguments

Printed the source and destination directories for verification.

echo "Target directory: $targetDirectory"
echo "Destination directory: $destinationDirectory"
![Task 2](screenshots/task2-display-directories.png)

Task 3: Generate Current Timestamp

Generated a Unix timestamp.

currentTS=$(date +%s)
![Task 3](screenshots/task3-current-timestamp.png)

Task 4: Create Backup Filename

Created a unique backup filename using the timestamp.

backupFileName="backup-$currentTS.tar.gz"

Example:

backup-1748539200.tar.gz
![Task 4](screenshots/task4-Set_Value.png)

Task 5: Get Current Directory Path

Stored the absolute path of the current working directory.

origAbsPath=$(pwd)
![Task 5](screenshots/task5-Define_Variable.png)

Task 6: Get Destination Directory Path

Changed to the destination directory and stored its absolute path.

cd "$destinationDirectory"
destDirAbsPath=$(pwd)
![Task 6](screenshots/task6-Define_Variable.png)

Task 7: Navigate to Target Directory

Returned to the original directory and entered the target directory.

cd "$origAbsPath"
cd "$targetDirectory"
![Task 7](screenshots/task7-Change_Directory.png)

Task 8: Calculate Yesterday's Timestamp

Calculated the timestamp from 24 hours ago.

yesterdayTS=$(($currentTS - 24 * 60 * 60))
![Task 8](screenshots/task8-YesterdayTS_.png)

Task 9: Iterate Through Files

Looped through every file and directory.

for file in *
![Task 9](screenshots/task9-List_AllFilesandDirectoriess.png)

Task 10: Check File Modification Time

Determined whether a file was modified within the last 24 hours.

if [[ `date -r $file +%s` -gt $yesterdayTS ]]
![Task 10](screenshots/task10-If_Statement.png)

Task 11: Add Files to Backup Array

Added qualifying files to an array.

toBackup+=($file)
![Task 11](screenshots/task11-Add_File.png)

Task 12: Create Backup Archive

Compressed all selected files.

tar -czvf $backupFileName ${toBackup[@]}
![Task 12](screenshots/task12-Create_Backup.png)

Task 13: Move Backup Archive

Moved the archive to the destination directory.

mv $backupFileName $destDirAbsPath
![Task 13](screenshots/task13-Move_Backup.png)

Task 14: Download Project Files

Downloaded the lab files.

wget https://cf-courses-data.s3.us.cloud-object-storage.appdomain.cloud/IBM-LX0117EN-SkillsNetwork/labs/Final%20Project/important-documents.zip

Task 15: Extract Files

Extracted the downloaded archive.

unzip -DDo important-documents.zip
![Task 15](screenshots/task15-executable.png)

Task 16: Update File Timestamps

Modified timestamps to simulate recent updates.

touch important-documents/*
![Task 16](screenshots/task16-backup-complete.png)

Task 17: Install Script and Automate Execution

Made the script executable.

chmod +x backup.sh

Installed globally.

sudo cp backup.sh /usr/local/bin/

Created a Cron Job.

crontab -e

Added:

*/1 * * * * /usr/local/bin/backup.sh /home/project/important-documents /home/project

Verified Cron Jobs.

crontab -l

▶️ Running the Project

Make the script executable:

chmod +x backup.sh

Run the script:

./backup.sh important-documents .

Check generated backup files:

ls -l *.tar.gz

View archive contents:

tar -tzvf backup-*.tar.gz

